// BUG-006 regression (fixed v0.0.5): VM ArrayPush instruction crashed with
// "expected Array, got String" when the LEFT operand of `$+` was a String.
//
// Root cause: zymbol-compiler always emits ArrayPush for CollectionAppend ($+)
// regardless of operand type. The VM's ArrayPush handler only covered
// Value::Array and Value::Tuple — any other type hit the default arm and
// raised a TypeError.
//
// The tree-walker was unaffected because it evaluates $+ dynamically and
// branches on the left-operand type at runtime.
//
// Discovered in klingon/HUD.zy — int-to-pIqaD converter prepended digits
// left-to-right with `s = d $+ s` where both d and s are Strings.
//
// Fix: added Value::String arm to ArrayPush fast-path and slow-path handlers
// in crates/zymbol-vm/src/lib.rs — concatenates the right-hand value's
// string representation to the string register.

// 1. Prepend: string on both sides (the original HUD.zy pattern)
s = ""
s = "b" $+ s
s = "a" $+ s
>> s ¶

// 2. Append: string $+ string (same operator, symmetric)
t = "hello"
t = t $+ " world"
>> t ¶

// 3. String $+ char
u = "hola"
u = u $+ '!'
>> u ¶

// 4. Build digit string right-to-left (exact HUD.__() pattern)
build_rev(n) {
    ? n == 0 { <~ "" }
    s = ""
    @:lup {
        ? n == 0 { @:lup! }
        r = n % 10
        d = "{r}"
        s = d $+ s
        n = n / 10
    }
    <~ s
}

>> build_rev(0) ¶
>> build_rev(7) ¶
>> build_rev(42) ¶
>> build_rev(123) ¶

// 5. Mixed: array $+ elem still works (no regression)
arr = [10, 20]
arr = arr $+ 30
>> arr[1] ¶
>> arr[2] ¶
>> arr[3] ¶
